","1. **Convert the concentration to a percentage-free-per-volume ratio**:  
   The concentration is 0.044% (w/v), which means 0.044 grams of sodium fluoride are present in 1000 volume of water (since the percentage is a percentage percent).  

2. **Calculate the mass of sodium fluoride in 10 mL**:  
   Set up a proportion:  
   \[
   \frac{0.044 \text{ g}}{1000 \text{ mL}} = \frac{x \text{ g}}{10 \text{ mL}}
   \]  
   Cross-multiply and solve for \(x\):  
   \[
   10 \text{ mL} \times 0.044 \text{ g} = 0.4 \text{ g} \times 1000 \text{ mL}
   \]  
   \[
   x = \frac{0.4 \text{ g} \times 10 \text{ mL}}{1000 \text{ mL}} = 0.044 \text{ g}
   \]  

3. **Convert grams to milligrams**:  
   1 gram = 1000 milligrams  
   \[
   0.044 \text{ g} \times 1000 \text{ mg/g} = 44 \text{ mg}
   \]  

**Final Answer:**  
