","Let the side length of the cube is $2$. Let the radius of the nine cubes be $r$. The center of the cube is at the origin $(1, 1, 1)$. The center of the central sphere is at the origin $(1, 1, 1)$. Since the cube has side length $2$, the vertices of the cube are $(0, 0, 0)$, $(2, 0, 0)$, $(0, 2, 0)$, $(0, 0, 2)$, $(2, 2, 0)$, $(2, 0, 2)$, $(0, 2, 2)$, and $(2, 2, 2)$.

The center of the central sphere is at $(1, 1, 1)$. Since the cube has side length $2$, the vertices of the cube are $(0, 0, 0)$, $(2, 0, 0)$, $(0, 2, 0)$, $(0, 0, 2)$, $(2, 2, 0)$, $(2, 0, 2)$, $(0, 2, 2)$, and $(2, 2, 2)$. The cube has side length $2$, so the volume of the cube is $2^3 = 8$.

The center of the central sphere is at the center of the cube, which is $(1, 1, 1)$. The center of one sphere is at $(1, 1, 1)$. This sphere touches only one other sphere, which touches three faces of the cube. Let the coordinates of the center of this sphere is $(r, r, r)$. Since the sphere is tangent to three faces of the cube, its center is at $(r, r, r)$. The distance between the center of the central sphere and the point $(r, r, r)$ is $2r$. Using the distance formula, we have:
\[
\sqrt{(1 - r)^2 + (1 - r)^2 + (1 - r)^2} = 2r \implies \sqrt{3(1 - r)^2} = 2r \implies \sqrt{3} |1 - r| = 2r.
