Yellow light travels 0.680 times as fast in a certain type of plastic than in a vacuum. What is the index of refraction for yellow light in the plastic?,"<bos><start_of_turn>user
Yellow light travels 0.680 times as fast in a certain type of plastic than in a vacuum. What is the index of refraction for yellow light in the plastic?<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>model
","The index of refraction \( n \) is defined as the ratio of the speed of light in a vacuum \( c \), to the speed of light in the medium \( v \):
\[
n = \frac{c}{v}
\]
Given that the light travels 0.680 times faster in the plastic than in a vacuum, the speed of light in the plastic is \( 0.680 \times c \). Substituting this into the formula:
\[
n = \frac{c}{0.680 \times c} = \frac{1}{0.680} \approx 1.46
\]
Thus, the index of refraction for yellow light in the plastic is \(\boxed{1.46}\).",relevance,"# Task Description
