","The scattered particle is assumed to have negligible mass, so the initial and final momenta are given by:
\[
P_i = \left( \frac{E_i}{c}, \mathbf{p}_i \right), \quad P_f = \left( \frac{E_f}{c}, \mathbf{p}_f \right).
\]
The momentum transfer \( \mathbf{q} \) is the difference between the initial and final momenta:
\[
\mathbf{q} = \mathbf{P}_f - \mathbf{P}_i = \mathbf{p}_f - \mathbf{p}_i.
\]
The squared momentum transfer \( Q^2 \) is the square of this vector:
\[
Q^2 = \mathbf{q} \cdot \mathbf{q} = \left( \mathbf{p}_f - \mathbf{p}_i \right) \cdot \left( \mathbf{p}_f - \mathbf{p}_i \right).
\]
