   The altitude of the isosilateral triangle is the longest segment connecting the midpoint of the base to the midpoint of the base. The altitude divides the triangle into two right triangles. 
   The hypotenuse of each right triangle is 15, and the hypotenuse is the length of the diagonal. The hypotenuse is 15, and one side is half of the base, which is 10. 
   Using the Pythagorean theorem:
   \[
